From d8a7d4c2d13a639ab41ab6c266718e054bf42dda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mick <sirmick@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 17:56:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Unicorn m68k: MacPhoenix host-integration patches

Collected 68k deltas that predate the PPC patch series and were
historically committed directly into mac-phoenix's vendored Unicorn
tree rather than tracked as standalone patches. Extracted here so
the full series reproduces the vendored state from pristine 2.1.4.

Per-file:

- qemu/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
  * M68K A-line opcode pre-read on exception_index==10: fetches the
    instruction word before the interrupt handler runs so
    cpu_m68k_exec_interrupt can inspect the unimplemented opcode
    (used by the MacPhoenix EmulOp dispatch path).
  * EXCP_RTE (0x100) fast-return: skip cpu_loop_exit_noexc on guest
    RTE so the emulator stays on the TCG main loop instead of
    unwinding to the C caller.
  * CHECKLOAD counter (g_cpu_exec_checkload_count) read by the
    MacPhoenix boot-progress tracker.
  * TB-lookup perf counters (g_tb_find_count/g_tb_miss_count/
    g_tb_buffer_flush_count) read by unicorn_wrapper.c.

- qemu/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
  * Bump g_tb_buffer_flush_count in tb_flush.

- qemu/target/m68k/cpu.h
  * Expose m68k_interrupt_all() for the non-static call from
    uc_m68k_trigger_interrupt.

- qemu/target/m68k/op_helper.c
  * Un-static m68k_interrupt_all and auto-ack hardware IRQs so
    guest timer/VBL interrupts are delivered in emulator-driven
    flows where no external interrupt controller runs.

- qemu/target/m68k/unicorn.c
  * uc_m68k_trigger_interrupt() helper called from the MacPhoenix
    timer thread.
  * SR read preserves cc_op so reading SR mid-TB doesn't clobber
    deferred condition-code state.

- qemu/target/m68k/translate.c
  * Loosen use_goto_tb: allow chaining for all branches (including
    backward/loops). Interrupt delivery switched to cpu_exit() +
    exit_request, which breaks goto_tb chains on demand.
  * gen_jmp_tb: sync cc_op to env->cc_op before leaving this TB,
    bypassing update_cc_op's cc_op_synced tracking because
    gen_jmpcc calls gen_jmp_tb twice.

All globals introduced here are non-weak; patch 0001 promotes them
to __attribute__((weak)) once ppc-softmmu.a joins the link.
